\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{The zero-sum constraint and the quartic}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{In \ref{fdip-0046}, a general eliminated quartic can produce
a sextic term at second order. In a hierarchical block the
fluctuation lies in the zero-sum subspace of \ref{fdip-01DE}.
Expanding the [Wick powers](fdip-01CV) by \ref{fdip-01CX} makes
that constraint visible before any coupling is truncated. Which
contractions can remain in the second-order polynomial?}
